---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import SectionHero from '../../components/SectionHero.astro'
import DocsMeta from '../../components/DocsMeta.astro'
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro'
import { ThemedShot } from '../../components/ThemedShot'
import { withBase } from '../../lib/path'
---
<DocsLayout title="Home" description="The landing page, built around the book you are reading: Resume, the other books in progress, the next volumes, your numbers, new arrivals, a highlight and recent activity.">
  <SectionHero section="features" />
  <h1>Home</h1>
  <p>
    Home is Tome's landing tab. It is built around the book you are reading now, with the rest of
    your reading life below it: the other books in progress, the next volumes of the series, a
    handful of numbers, what was added to the library, a highlight, and your recent sessions.
  </p>
  <DocsMeta />

  <h2>The book you are reading</h2>
  <p>
    The top of the page is your most recently synced in-progress book: its cover, the series and
    volume above the title, the author, the start of the description, and your progress. <strong>Resume</strong> opens it in the <a href={withBase("/docs/reader")}>web reader</a> at your
    position; the line beside it says where the position came from and when (for example
    "Synced from KOReader · 2 hours ago"). The series name links to the series page, the cover and
    the title to the book page.
  </p>

  <h2>Also reading and Up next</h2>
  <p>
    Under the hero, <strong>Also reading</strong> is a row of your other books in progress, each
    with a thin progress bar. Click a cover to bring that book up as the hero; when there are more
    than fit, the last tile takes you to the Library filtered to books you are reading. <strong>Up next</strong> sits beside it and shows the next volumes of the hero's series, with a
    count of how many are still ahead.
  </p>
  <div class="docs-shot">
    <ThemedShot client:load name="home-hero" alt="Home: the book being read as a hero with progress and Resume, Also reading on the left and the next volumes of its series under Up next" />
  </div>

  <h2>The numbers</h2>
  <p>
    A strip of four numbers: your reading <strong>streak</strong> (days, or weeks when you read
    every week but not every day, with your best), time read <strong>this month</strong>, books <strong>finished</strong> in the last 30 days, and the size of the <strong>library</strong>. If
    you have set <a href={withBase("/docs/stats")}>reading goals</a>, their progress rings sit under
    the strip; click one to open Stats.
  </p>
  <div class="docs-shot">
    <ThemedShot client:load name="home-numbers" alt="The four numbers on Home: streak, time read this month, books finished in the last 30 days, and library size" />
  </div>
  <p>
    The fuller picture, including the Reading DNA reading personality, is on the <a href={withBase("/docs/stats")}>Stats</a> page (Reading DNA is a tile you add from <strong>Add tile</strong> under Habits).
  </p>

  <h2>Recently added and the quick look</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Recently added</strong> is a row of the newest books in the library; <strong>See all</strong> opens the Library sorted by date added. Clicking a cover here, in Up next, or in any grid or row
    in Tome opens the <strong>quick look</strong>: the cover, series, title, author and description,
    your progress and reading time when you have started the book, and <strong>Resume</strong> (or <strong>Read</strong>) and <strong>Open page</strong>, without leaving the page you are on.
    Escape or a click outside closes it.
  </p>
  <div class="docs-shot">
    <ThemedShot client:load name="home-quick-look" alt="The quick look over Home: a recently added book's cover, title, author and description with Read and Open page" />
  </div>

  <h2>Upcoming releases</h2>
  <p>
    When a series you follow has a next volume with a known release date, Home lists it under <strong>Upcoming releases</strong>, soonest first. Following itself lives on the <a href={withBase("/docs/wishlist")}>Wishlist</a> page's <strong>Following</strong> strip and on
    each series page's <strong>Follow</strong> button; it needs release detection to be on.
  </p>

  <h2>A highlight</h2>
  <p>
    Home shows one of your highlights: one you made on this day in an earlier month or year when
    there is one (<strong>On this day</strong>), otherwise a random one (<strong>From your
    highlights</strong>). The shuffle button shows another, <strong>All</strong> opens your <a href={withBase("/docs/highlights")}>commonplace book</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Recent activity</h2>
  <p>
    The last reading sessions as plain rows: the book, the number of sessions, time and pages, and
    how long ago. Back-to-back sessions of the same book on the same day share one row. <strong>See all</strong> opens <a href={withBase("/docs/stats")}>Stats</a>.
  </p>

  <Callout variant="note" title="Which books count as 'in progress'?">
    The hero and Also reading draw from per-user reading status: books marked <strong>reading</strong>, whether that status came from the web reader, KOReader sync, or a
    manual change on the book page.
  </Callout>
</DocsLayout>
